// Sustained single-target lightning beam (concentration), the school's own
// first `BasicBeam` player-spell precedent at circle 1 -- the only shipped
// siblings (exsanguinate circle 5, gravity_fissure circle 6) run much
// shorter `beam_duration` (3-4s) with a very high `energy_drain` (137-162,
// i.e. energy/sec while channeling) that burns through most builds' energy
// pool in ~1s regardless of the nominal cap. `beam_duration: 60` here
// matches the sheet's `Concentration(60)` (D&D's "up to 1 minute") as the
// hard cap, but `energy_drain: 18` is deliberately low so a circle-1 caster
// can actually sustain it for several seconds rather than have the 60s cap
// be purely cosmetic -- self-gates reuse via the drain, so no separate
// `cooldown` is set (matches every other circle-0/1 spell in this batch).
// Flagged for wave-close-out balance review alongside burning_hands/
// thunderwave (no circle-1 BasicBeam sibling to calibrate against yet).
BasicBeam(
    buildup_duration: 0.4,
    recover_duration: 0.35,
    beam_duration: 60,
    damage: 6.0,
    tick_rate: 3.0,
    range: 9.0,
    max_angle: 5.0,
    damage_effect: None,
    energy_regen: 0,
    energy_drain: 18,
    move_efficiency: 0.3,
    ori_rate: 0.3,
    specifier: Lightning,
    meta: (school: Some(Evocation), source: Some(Arcane)),
)
